-- int-tests-contravention: headline (c), whole scenarios across groups G1 (misconduct, Article 2(10); the entity), G2 (the charity test), G3 (the principal address, for Article 11(4)(d)), G4 (Article 11(4)(c), (d)),
-- G5 (the court's powers, Article 14), G6 (Articles 16 to 19: deregistration and its effects, governors' misconduct and reportable matters), G7 (Article 22; commencement; the text) and G8 (required steps notices,
-- Article 27; IP19), G9 (IP28).  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run:
--   Article 2(10)(a)(i): "misconduct" means a contravention by a registered charity or any of its governors of a provision of this Law; Article 18(4)(a): a governor engages in misconduct if the governor
--   contravenes a provision of this Law or commits an offence within 2(10); Article 27(1): if the Commissioner believes there has been misconduct by a registered charity, that it does not pass the charity test,
--   that a governor has engaged in misconduct, that a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter, or that it has ceased to meet 11(4)(c) or (d), the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice (27(2));
--   Article 16(1): the Commissioner may deregister if satisfied, after a preliminary notice giving reasons and inviting objections, that (a) it no longer meets the charity test, (b) it misled, (c) it has failed to
--   comply with a required steps notice, (d) a prescribed circumstance; Article 17(1)(a): the Commissioner must retain the information registered for 10 years after deregistering; Article 14(1): on application by the
--   Commissioner or the Attorney General the court may exercise its powers if there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity, or it is necessary or desirable to protect its property.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (c): scenarios`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      expected IS A LIST OF a
      actual IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the same items` expected actual MEANS
        count expected EQUALS count actual
    AND all (GIVEN x YIELD elem x actual) expected

GIVETH A `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)`
`what appears to the court when the conduct concerns the administration` MEANS
    `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS TRUE, `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE, `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)`
`what appears to the court when nothing is amiss` MEANS
    `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS FALSE, `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE, `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

-- The base case: the registered school company, no contravention, an office filled, the court asked by the Commissioner.
GIVETH A `Contravention case`
`the case with no contravention` MEANS
    `Contravention case` WITH
        charity IS `Int fx the register entry of the school company`
        contraventions IS EMPTY
        conduct IS `Int fx conduct that contravenes nothing`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `Int fx the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `conduct of the governors` IS LIST (`Int fx a governor whose conduct is clear called` "A. Le Brun")
        `the Commissioner's beliefs` IS EMPTY
        `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` IS FALSE
        `facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` IS `Int fx proportionate to deregister`
        `preliminary notice` IS NOTHING
        deregistration IS NOTHING
        `application to the court` IS `an application by the Commissioner`
        `what appears to the court` IS `what appears to the court when nothing is amiss`
        `the charity carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS TRUE
        `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` IS FALSE
        `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act` IS FALSE
        `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` IS FALSE

§§ `C1: nothing has gone wrong -- no contravention, no misconduct, no ground, no power`

#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `a provision of this Law has been contravened`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `the governors who engage in misconduct within Article 18(4)` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `a ground of Article 16(1) for deregistration exists`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable on the Commissioner's application`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `someone is acting as the Commissioner`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the case with no contravention`)'s `the effects of the deregistration` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `C2: a governor acts after reporting a reportable matter without permission -- Article 19(10) -- which is misconduct, and gives the Commissioner and the court their powers`

-- Reported to the Commissioner on 1 March 2026; acted on 1 April 2026; no permission. Article 19(10) is contravened (a contravention of a provision of this Law: IP13), which is misconduct by a governor of a registered charity
-- (Article 2(10)(a)(i)), so the governor engages in misconduct (Article 18(4)(a)); the Commissioner may believe there has been misconduct and that a governor has engaged in it (Article 27(1)(a) and (c)).
GIVETH A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
`the position of a governor who reported on 1 March 2026` MEANS
    `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` WITH
        `the matter arose on` IS YMD 2026 2 20
        `the governor became aware of the matter on` IS YMD 2026 2 22
        `reported to the entity or charity on` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
        `reported to the Commissioner on` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
        `the reports were made promptly` IS TRUE
        `a prompt time has run out` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Contravention of this Law in the case`
`the governor acted after reporting` MEANS
    `a person acted as a governor after reporting a reportable matter` WITH position IS `the position of a governor who reported on 1 March 2026`, permissions IS EMPTY, `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Governor conduct in the case`
`the conduct of the governor who acted after reporting` MEANS
    `Governor conduct in the case` WITH conduct IS `Int fx the clear conduct of` "A. Le Brun", `own conduct facts` IS `Int fx conduct by a registered charity or its governor`, `own contraventions` IS LIST `the governor acted after reporting`

GIVETH A `Contravention case`
`the case of the governor who acted after reporting` MEANS
    `Int fx the contravention case with the Commissioner's beliefs replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with what appears to the court replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with conduct of the governors replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with conduct replaced` (`Int fx the contravention case with contraventions replaced` `the case with no contravention` (LIST `the governor acted after reporting`)) `Int fx conduct by a registered charity or its governor`) (LIST `the conduct of the governor who acted after reporting`)) `what appears to the court when the conduct concerns the administration`) (LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`, `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`)

#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) `the case of the governor who acted after reporting`)'s `a provision of this Law has been contravened`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) `the case of the governor who acted after reporting`)'s `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) `the case of the governor who acted after reporting`)'s `the governors who engage in misconduct within Article 18(4)` EQUALS LIST "A. Le Brun"
#ASSERT `the same items` (LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`, `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`) ((`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) `the case of the governor who acted after reporting`)'s `the grounds on which the Commissioner may serve a required steps notice`)
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) `the case of the governor who acted after reporting`)'s `the powers of the court under Article 14 are exercisable on the Commissioner's application`
-- Before the report (28 February 2026) nothing was contravened: the same case, asked about that day, shows no contravention by the governor.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 2 28) `the case of the governor who acted after reporting`)'s `a provision of this Law has been contravened`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 2 28) `the case of the governor who acted after reporting`)'s `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`

-- The Commissioner's power to serve a required steps notice on the charity, on belief (a): open (a permission that stands), and used when the Commissioner serves.
