§§ `C7: an offence in relation to an excepted foreign charity -- Article 2(10)(b) -- is misconduct only if the entity is an excepted foreign charity (Article 22; IP26)`

-- Article 2(10)(b): the commission by any person, in relation to a registered charity, to an excepted foreign charity (within the meaning of Article 22) or to an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of another
-- jurisdiction, of an offence involving deception or dishonesty (clause (v)).  The entity here is not on the register and is not equivalent under any other jurisdiction's law, so the only way the limb can be met is by Article 22.
-- Article 22: an entity established under the law of the United Kingdom, entitled there to call itself a charity and managed from there, is an excepted foreign charity; an otherwise identical entity established under Jersey law is not.
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`a body that is not on the register` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH name IS "Cotswold Aid Limited", standing IS `not on the register`, purposes IS ((`Int fx the registered school company`)'s purposes), facts IS `Int fx a foreign body similar to` (LIST `a company`), model IS `Int fx clear model facts`, people IS EMPTY
GIVETH A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test`
`the facts of a body established in the United Kingdom, a charity there and managed from there` MEANS
    `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH `established under` IS `the law of the United Kingdom or of a jurisdiction that is part of the United Kingdom`, `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS TRUE, `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS TRUE, `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
`conduct that is a dishonesty offence in relation to the entity` MEANS
    `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)` WITH
        `standing of the entity when the conduct occurred` IS `not on the register`
        `standing of the entity when the question is asked` IS `not on the register`
        `the constitutional Laws of the charity` IS EMPTY
        `an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS FALSE
        `by the registered charity or by one of its governors` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of the constitution of the registered charity` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of a required steps notice` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under this Law` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under this Law` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS FALSE
        `the offence is in relation to the entity` IS TRUE
        `an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity` IS FALSE
        `an offence under the financial services Laws, any Regulation or Order made under them, or the Alternative Investment Funds (Jersey) Regulations 2012` IS FALSE
        `an offence under the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961, the Goods and Services Tax (Jersey) Law 2007 or the Taxation (Land Transactions) (Jersey) Law 2009` IS FALSE
        `an offence under any other enactment relating to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS FALSE
        `an offence under any other enactment or under customary law involving deception or dishonesty` IS TRUE
        `an offence under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey similar to one listed in (i) to (v)` IS FALSE
GIVEN excepted IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc The facts Article 22 reads
GIVETH A `Contravention case`
`the case of an offence in relation to a body not on the register, with` excepted MEANS
    `Contravention case` WITH
        charity IS `Int fx the register entry with body replaced` `Int fx the register entry of the school company` `a body that is not on the register`
        contraventions IS EMPTY
        conduct IS `conduct that is a dishonesty offence in relation to the entity`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS excepted
        `conduct of the governors` IS EMPTY
        `the Commissioner's beliefs` IS EMPTY
        `a governor is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` IS FALSE
        `facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` IS `Int fx proportionate to deregister`
        `preliminary notice` IS NOTHING
        deregistration IS NOTHING
        `application to the court` IS `an application by the Commissioner`
        `what appears to the court` IS `what appears to the court when nothing is amiss`
        `the charity carries out, or intends to carry out, an activity in or from within Jersey` IS FALSE
        `the activity is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, substantial` IS FALSE
        `a relevant person has been designated under sub-paragraph (4)` IS FALSE
        `the person appointed as the Commissioner is unable to act` IS FALSE
        `there is a vacancy in the office of Commissioner` IS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the case of an offence in relation to a body not on the register, with` `the facts of a body established in the United Kingdom, a charity there and managed from there`))'s `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`the case of an offence in relation to a body not on the register, with` `Int fx the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`))'s `the charity's conduct is misconduct within Article 2(10)`

§§ `C6: the day -- Articles 14 to 20 and 27 were in force from 1 May 2018, Article 22 only from 1 January 2019`

-- On 31 December 2018 the first Article in the list that is not in force is Article 22 (Part 6; trap T30: Article 2(10)(b) cites it).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2018 12 31) `the case with no contravention` BECAUSE "Article 22 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (c) what follows from the contravention` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30) `the case with no contravention` BECAUSE "Article 12 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
